VeridianOS: no partial designated initializers

GCC warns in C++ for every member a designated initializer leaves out
(-Wmissing-field-initializers; in C it does not), 209 times across these
files: output states and information, DRM, Vulkan and sync_file ioctl
structs, render nodes, transaction entries. Each such object is now
value-initialized with empty braces -- which gives every member its
default member initializer or zero, exactly what the omitted designators
gave -- and the named members are assigned after it, in the same order.
RenderContext has const members, which cannot be assigned, so its
initializer names its remaining members instead. sync_merge_data's name is
a char array, copied with strncpy into the zeroed struct (NUL-terminated,
as before).

ColorSurfaceFeedback's listener names the protocol's version 2 event,
preferred_changed2, as null: the color manager is bound at version 1, so
the event is never sent (and a listener member left out is null too).

